id=lxxrahlfsplus
short.title=LXX Rahlfs+
title=Septuagint (Rahlfs) with Strong's numbers and CATSS morphology
title.english=Septuagint (Rahlfs) with Strong's numbers and CATSS morphology
lang=grc
description=The Greek Old Testament (Septuagint), Rahlfs text, every word tagged with Strong's number, CATSS morphology and lemma
author=Rahlfs, Alfred; Valdez, Edmund
publisher=Edmund Paulino Valdez
version.major=1
version.minor=11
version.date=2026-11-20
morph.dct=d5-mx
strongs.g.dct=jb51
creator=Edmund Valdez
source=CATSS LXX Morphology (lxxmorph), Center for Computer Analysis of Texts, University of Pennsylvania
font=Gentium,GentiumAlt,Cardo,Palatino Linotype
about=<CENTER><b>LXX Rahlfs+</b><br>The Greek Old Testament (Septuagint)<br>Rahlfs text, fully tagged</CENTER><br>\
<b>Text, morphology and lemmas:</b> the CATSS morphologically analysed Septuagint (Rahlfs 1935), as in the LXX Morph module (lxxmorph-rc). Morphology codes are Packard's CATSS codes, defined in <i>Packard's and Robinson's Morphological Analysis Codes</i>.<br><br>\
<b>Strong's numbers:</b> every Greek word carries a Strong's number: standard Strong's/Thayer numbers (G1-G5624) wherever the word is the same as a New Testament word, and the Septuagint numbers of the companion dictionary <i>Bible Greek Definitions</i> (epv-thayer-kjv_dct.twm) for the rest, the same numbers used in LXX Brenton+ and SweteLXX+. Words found only in Rahlfs carry new numbers from G12942.<br><br>\
<b>How the numbers were assigned:</b> each Rahlfs word was matched with the same word in LXX Brenton+, in the same verse or a neighbouring one; the remaining words by their CATSS lemma, the dictionary headword, or by hand. Every number was then checked against its dictionary headword, and Brenton+ tags that belong to a different word were corrected.<br><br>\
<b>Verse numbers:</b> KJV versification; the blue superscript (toggle z) shows the CATSS reference, and the red superscript shows the Septuagint reference where it differs.<br><br>\
<b>Verses added in version 1.4:</b> 249 verses that the LXX Morph module left empty (chiefly Proverbs 25&ndash;29, which CATSS numbers 32&ndash;36, and parts of Jeremiah and 1 Kings 20) were filled from <i>LXX-Rahlfs-1935</i> by Eliran Wong (github.com/eliranwong/LXX-Rahlfs-1935, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), a derivative of the same CCAT data; their Strong&rsquo;s numbers come from Swete and Brenton in the same verse. Eight verses that the LXX Morph module repeated on two lines (version 1.3) appear only once. Non-commercial use only, as the CCAT user agreement requires.<br><br>\
<b>Hover pop-ups:</b> hover over any Greek word to see its Strong's number, lemma and grammar code.<br><br>\
<b>Books:</b> the 39 books of the Hebrew canon only; the other books of Rahlfs' edition (Tobit, Judith, 1–4 Maccabees, Wisdom, Sirach, etc.) are not included.<br><br>\
<b>Version 1.1 (2026-10-21):</b> Strong's numbers made consistent for the separately numbered forms of ἐγώ, σύ, εἰμί, λέγω/εἶπον, ὁράω and μιμνῄσκω (e.g. σου G4675, μοι G3427, ἔσται G2071); wrong numbers and broken lemmas corrected; Rahlfs-only words given dictionary entries (G12942–G13143); malformed morph codes fixed; half-verse markers (e.g. 29a) can be hidden with toggle z.<br><br>\
Module tagging by Edmund Valdez.
